9:The frontmatter the model fills on each source page is the input to the routing layer described in CLAUDE.md Part 5b. Routing fan-out, ingredient `contamination_profile` updates, and product-page table regeneration all depend on this frontmatter being accurate and at the right level of specificity.
15:The **filesystem handle** is the `FM_XXXXXXX` identifier. Stable, globally unique, collision-free. Used for `raw/markdown/` folder names, the `raw_handle` frontmatter field, and cross-references that need to be unambiguous across Claude sessions. Claude must never change or re-derive a filesystem handle.
19:When the triage manifest provides a cite-key, use it. When it does not, derive one from first author, year, and a short topic slug, then record it in source-page frontmatter. If two papers generate the same cite-key, append `-a`, `-b`, etc. Prefer the manifest's pre-populated cite-key over re-deriving on the fly, to prevent inconsistency across sessions.
23:Every ingested file produces exactly one source page at `wiki/sources/<cite-key>.md`. Frontmatter includes both identifiers:
26:raw_handle: FM_3750310
36:For **exact duplicates**, ingest only one file. Log the skip to `log.md`: `## [YYYY-MM-DD] skip | FM_XXXXX is SHA-identical to FM_YYYYY, not ingested`. Keep both files in `raw/markdown/` — storage is cheap and preserving both protects against dedup-logic errors.
38:For **near-duplicates** (papers flagged in the manifest's cluster column), prefer the higher-evidence-tier version. Published versions beat preprints; peer-reviewed versions beat conference abstracts. Create one source page for the preferred version. Note the relationship in frontmatter:
49:raw_handle: FM_XXXXXXX
65:Source-page frontmatter is the routing layer's input. The model is responsible for declaring `products:` and `ingredients:` against the **existing** wiki taxonomy, not inventing slugs from the paper's text. Before writing any source page, check `wiki/products/` and `wiki/ingredients/` to know what slugs exist. Declared slugs are selected from that vocabulary; new slugs are not invented mid-ingest.
71:When the model writes the source page, it does not auto-create destination pages. Sources referencing an ingredient slug that doesn't exist surface as a `routing_unresolved.csv` entry; the autonomy loop's `tools/autonomy/create-missing-pages.mjs` creates ingredient stubs at frequency >= 2. Sources referencing a product slug that doesn't exist also surface in `routing_unresolved.csv` but the autonomy loop does **not** create the product stub — product pages are HMTc governance units requiring Karen's Step 0 Lock plus a scaffold-script commit. See CLAUDE.md Part 10 and `docs/order-of-operations.md` for the workflow.
83:For this build, ingest means compiling a source into the persistent wiki system. It does not mean "the file is searchable now." The work is split across actors: **model** writes prose (source pages, narrative wiki content where appropriate); **system** scripts handle routing and structured-evidence emission; **generators** rebuild product-page tables and other compiled views; **Karen** decides scope, names new pages, and approves limit-setting work.
88:2. [model] create or update the canonical source page at `wiki/sources/<cite-key>.md`, filling in frontmatter accurately (especially `products`, `ingredients`, `matrices`, `metals`, `jurisdictions`).
99:When Karen drops a file into `raw/` and says "ingest this", the model's deliverable is the source page plus a list of any new pages the routing layer flags as unresolved. Routing fan-out, ingredient `contamination_profile` updates, and product-page table regeneration are downstream system passes, not part of the ingest itself.
103:3. [model] Create the source page using the template in [[docs/page-templates]]. Frontmatter accuracy is load-bearing because it feeds the routing layer; fill `products`, `ingredients`, `matrices`, `metals`, `jurisdictions` at the level of specificity the source actually states.
104:4. [system] Rebuild the routing audit by running `npm run evidence:source-routes` (or letting the watcher pick up the new source page). The audit names the affected product, ingredient, metal, and regulation pages.
120:4. Commit after each batch of 200, not per-paper. A single commit per batch: `ingest batch 03 (papers 401-600): 47 source pages added`.
123:   - New source pages created (list of cite-keys)
130:**The model's only output during bulk ingest is source pages.** Bulk ingest sessions do not edit product-category page tables, do not edit `data/evidence/product_source_routing_audit.csv`, do not edit `data/evidence/values.jsonl`, and do not advance `contamination_profile` blocks on ingredient pages. Those layers are downstream artifacts. If a bulk session finds itself wanting to update a product page or routing audit by hand, that is a signal to stop and surface the misunderstanding to Karen.
