214:### Source legend
241:The `Source Evidence Inventory` separates measured product concentrations from intake or exposure estimates. Shows what each source actually reports: metal, evidence scope, n, statistic type, reported values, units, max or p100 if directly reported, row-fit, brief evidence note. Do not add p10/p50/p90/p95 columns unless the source itself reports those.
245:Row-fit is a compound classification with two axes: **matrix axis** (milk-based vs soy-based vs hydrolyzed; rice-based vs non-rice; root vegetable vs leafy green) and **format axis** (powdered vs ready-to-feed vs concentrated liquid; dry vs as-consumed; jar vs pouch). Each axis is exact, partial, or unknown independently. Source-page TL;DR and frontmatter `matrices` / `products` should record both axes explicitly when known.
253:Inline and table citations on product-category pages use numbered aliases `[[sources/<cite-key>|1]]`. A `Sources` block at the end maps each number to the full source page.
